# Perl Backend Rules

Backend-focused integration from upstream `rules/perl/*`.

## Style
- Use `v5.36` for new backend code to enable strictness, warnings, `say`, and signatures.
- Use subroutine signatures instead of manual `@_` unpacking.
- Use Moo with read-only attributes and `Types::Standard` for DTOs/value objects.
- Use `perltidy` and `perlcritic` with core, PBP, and security themes.
- Use `cpanfile` plus `carton` for reproducible installs.

## Backend patterns
- Use DBI or DBIx::Class behind repository modules.
- Use Moo DTO/value-object classes instead of anonymous hashrefs for service boundaries.
- Use `autodie`, three-arg `open`, and Path::Tiny for file operations.
- Use `Exporter 'import'` with `@EXPORT_OK`; never export by default.

## Security
- Use taint mode (`-T`) for CGI/web-facing scripts.
- Sanitize `%ENV` before external commands.
- Untaint with allowlist regexes; never use catch-all `(.*)`.
- Prevent path traversal with `Cwd::realpath` and allowed-directory checks.
- Use list-form `system()` or IPC::Run3; never backticks with variable interpolation.
- Always use DBI placeholders; never interpolate values into SQL.
- Prefer framework/provider auth modules over custom password, session, or JWT
  implementations.

## Testing
- Use Test2::V0 for new tests.
- Run `prove -l t/` or `prove -lr -j8 t/`; always include `-l`.
- Use Devel::Cover for 80%+ coverage targets.
- Use Test::MockModule or Test::MockObject for test doubles.
